<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Ayyubid Emirate of Mayyafariqin</h1><p class="st-meta">1185 CE – 1260 CE · capital Mayyafariqin</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Ayyubid principality of Diyar Bakr, whose last prince died resisting the Mongols after a long siege in 1260.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayyafariqin">Mayyafariqin</a> in 1185 from the Shah-Armens' sphere; after a period under his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taqi-al-din-umar">Taqi al-Din</a> it passed to his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-adil">al-Adil</a>, whose son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-awhad-ayyub">al-Awhad Ayyub</a> ruled it and in 1207 took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahlat">Ahlat</a>. It became a hereditary Ayyubid principality in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-mesopotamia">Jazira</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The principality passed to al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-ashraf-musa-sultan-of-damascus">Ashraf Musa</a> and then to al-Muzaffar <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a>, sons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-adil">al-Adil</a>, and then to Ghazi's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil-muhammad-of-mayyafariqin">al-Kamil Muhammad</a>. Its rulers controlled the old <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marwanids">Marwanid</a> capital, rich farmland north of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a> and roads to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahlat">Ahlat</a>. They faced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmians">Khwarazmians</a>, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a> and finally the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil">Al-Kamil</a> Muhammad defied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hulagu-khan">Hulagu</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Mongol forces besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayyafariqin">Mayyafariqin</a> from 1259; in 1260 the city fell after famine, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil-muhammad-of-mayyafariqin">al-Kamil Muhammad</a> was killed and his head was paraded in Syrian cities.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1185 CE – 1260 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Anatolia and the Levant</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.28%;width:1.49%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1185 CE – 1260 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Mayyafariqin</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>al-Awhad Ayyub, al-Muzaffar Ghazi, al-Kamil Muhammad</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ayyubids of Diyar Bakr</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1222&amp;focus=ayyubid-emirate-of-mayyafariqin" aria-label="Ayyubid Emirate of Mayyafariqin on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5701 807 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ayyubid Emirate of Mayyafariqin lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6021 1063L5811 1337M6021 1063L6134 1224"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5811 1337h0M6134 1224h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6021 1063h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6021 1063h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Mayyafariqin. <a href="/atlas?year=1222&amp;focus=ayyubid-emirate-of-mayyafariqin">On the at